 "notes": "Headline result: dark photon (kinetic mixing eps=chi) SN1987A cooling bound, Figure 3 (SN.pdf in the arXiv e-print), the solid-black overall excluded region. Extracted as a vector path (fill path 11) and calibrated from the axis tick strokes: x 50.7px=0.1MeV to 436.7px=1000MeV (96.5px/decade), y 245.2px=1e-11 to 6.7px=1e-3 (29.8px/decade). Verified features: upper edge ~2.2e-4 at 0.1MeV with the sharp drop near 1MeV, lower reach dipping to ~6e-11 near 17MeV, right tip ~400MeV at ~7e-9. This is a CLOSED excluded region; points trace the full boundary loop (lower edge left->right, then upper edge right->left, closed) rather than a single-valued curve, clipped at the left axis (0.1MeV=1e5 eV). y-axis already the canonical chi; no conversion. Energy-loss (Raffelt) argument from a single representative SN model; paper stresses these are order-of-magnitude estimates and states no confidence level. Not a DM search, so no density assumed. Paper also derives B-L vector (Fig4), scalar-e/N (Fig5) and Higgs-portal scalar (Fig6) bounds; the dark-photon SN bound is presented as a main headline result.",
